The '''2024 FIFA Intercontinental Cup''' (officially known as the '''FIFA Intercontinental Cup Qatar 2024 presented by [[Saudi Aramco|Aramco]]''' for sponsorship reasons)<ref>{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/about-fifa/organisation/news/fifa-intercontinental-cup-2024-stadiums-revealed |title=FIFA Intercontinental Cup 2024 stadiums revealed |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=12 November 2024 |access-date=14 November 2024}}</ref> was the inaugural edition of the [[FIFA Intercontinental Cup]], an annual club [[association football]] tournament organised by [[FIFA]]. The tournament comprised the six teams that won the previous edition of the continental championships in each FIFA confederation, playing each other in a [[single-elimination]] bracket. It was held from 22 September to 18 December 2024. The first two games were played in the stadium of a team involved in each match, and the final three (including the [[2024 FIFA Intercontinental Cup final|final]]) were played in Qatar as a neutral venue.<ref name="FIFA">{{cite press release |date=17 December 2023 |title=FIFA Council confirms key details for FIFA Club World Cup 2025 |url=https://www.fifa.com/about-fifa/organisation/fifa-council/media-releases/fifa-council-confirms-key-details-for-fifa-club-world-cup-2025-tm |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |access-date=17 December 2023}}</ref>

The tournament broadly maintains the format of the previous annual versions of the [[FIFA Club World Cup]], which was expanded and reorganised into a quadrennial tournament with more entrants, with the exception of changes to venues for the initial rounds.<ref name="FIFA"/>

==Format==
The details were approved by the [[FIFA Council]] on 17 December 2023, with the format formally confirmed on 20 September 2024.<ref name="SportingNews">{{cite news |last=Bonn |first=Kyle |date=17 December 2023 |title=Club World Cup 2025 in USA: Confirmed teams, format, schedule, dates for FIFA tournament with expanded field |url=https://www.sportingnews.com/us/soccer/news/club-world-cup-2025-usa-teams-format-dates-schedule-fifa/d5370f31621951fc1e4499e7 |work=[[The Sporting News]] |access-date=17 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Nair |first=Rohith |date=17 December 2023 |title=Club World Cup set for June–July 2025, new Intercontinental Cup in 2024 –FIFA |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/club-world-cup-set-june-july-2025-new-intercontinental-cup-2024-fifa-2023-12-17/ |agency=[[Reuters]] |access-date=17 December 2023}}</ref><ref name="key info"/><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/intercontinentalcup/2024/articles/bureau-council-update |title=Bureau of the Council update on FIFA Intercontinental Cup 2024 |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=19 September 2024 |access-date=21 September 2024}}</ref>

* '''First round''': The winners of the [[2023–24 AFC Champions League]]{{efn|name="rounddraw"|A draw determined whether the winners of the [[2023–24 AFC Champions League]] or the [[2023–24 CAF Champions League]] would play in the first round. Consequently, the other team entered in the second round.}} hosted the winners of the [[2024 OFC Champions League]] in the "FIFA African–Asian–Pacific Cup play-off".<ref>{{Cite tweet |number=1828237517784785314 |user=AucklandCity_FC |title=Intercontinental Cup: City to face AFC Champs |date=26 August 2024}}</ref>
* '''Second round''': The winners of the [[2023–24 CAF Champions League]] hosted the winners of the first round for the title of the "FIFA African–Asian–Pacific Cup". In parallel, the winners of the [[2024 Copa Libertadores]] and the winners of the [[2024 CONCACAF Champions Cup]] played each other in [[Doha]], Qatar, in a match that will be denominated the "FIFA Derby of the Americas".
* '''Play-off''': The winners of the second round matches played each other in Doha, Qatar in the "FIFA Challenger Cup".
* '''Final''': The winners of the play-off (FIFA Challenger Cup) played the winners of the [[2023–24 UEFA Champions League]] in [[Lusail]], Qatar.

